<title>EGYPT: Egypt says buys 21,000 tonnes of sunflower oil.</title>
<headline>Egypt says buys 21,000 tonnes of sunflower oil.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's official Holding Company for Food Industries said on Tuesday it had bought 21,000 tonnes of crude sunflower oil in bulk for delivery in the second half of September.</p>
<p>Muharran Ghanem, head of the sales sector, told Reuters the purchases were as follows:</p>
<p>-- 3,000 tonnes from Glencore at $544.75.</p>
<p>-- Four shipments of 3,000 tonnes each from Glencore at $549.75.</p>
<p>-- 3,000 tonnes from Finagrain at $547.</p>
<p>-- 3,000 tonnes from Finagrain at $549.</p>
<p>$1= 3.395 pounds.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
